Falsifies `file_allocation_table::boot_sector::verification::the_fat_type_is_the_cluster_counts`.

The defect: the FAT12 ceiling is off by one, so a volume of exactly 4084 clusters is typed FAT16.
Its table holds 12-bit entries and the reader would decode them 16 bits at a time.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert!((4085..65525).contains(&clusters))`.

diff --git a/crates/file_allocation_table/src/boot_sector.rs b/crates/file_allocation_table/src/boot_sector.rs
index 9dc607eda..f428da782 100644
--- a/crates/file_allocation_table/src/boot_sector.rs
+++ b/crates/file_allocation_table/src/boot_sector.rs
@@ -11,7 +11,7 @@
 use crate::sector::{SectorDevice, SectorSize};
 
 /// The cluster count below which a volume is FAT12, by the specification's rule.
-const FAT16_MIN_CLUSTERS: u32 = 4085;
+const FAT16_MIN_CLUSTERS: u32 = 4084;
 
 /// The cluster count below which a volume is FAT16, and at or above which it is FAT32.
 const FAT32_MIN_CLUSTERS: u32 = 65_525;
